{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Stories From the Hospital", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Child Saved by Puppies", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals for Possibility and Certainty", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs. They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without \u2018to') of the main verb. <br/> Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or possibility. Some common modals are: <span class=\"italic\">might, may, could, would,</span> and <span class=\"italic\">must</span>. <br><span class=\"italic\"> Might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">May</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Could</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Would</span>  are used to talk about <span class=\"underline\">possibility</span>. <span class=\"italic\">Might</span> is less certain than <span class=\"italic\">May</span>. <br><span class=\"italic\">May</span> , <span class=\"italic\">Could </span> and <span class=\"italic\">Would</span> have similar degrees of possibility. <br> <span class=\"italic\">Must</span> is used to talk about <span class=\"underline\">certainty </span> (something is 100% certain). The short form of <span class=\"italic\">must not</span> is <span class=\"italic\">mustn't</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use modals with a variety of verb tenses. You can use them to talk about possible or certain actions in the present, past or future. <br/><br/>  You can use modals with the <span class=\"underline\">Simple Present tense</span>:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">This <span class=\"strong\">might be</span> the most uncanny, but most heartwarming story of the year so far.</span><br/> (Here, the modal <span class=\"italic\">might</span> adds the meaning of <span class=\"strong\">possibility</span>:<br/>  It is possible that this is the most uncanny story of the year.)<br/><br/>  You can use modals with <span class=\"underline\">have+past participle </span> to talk about the possibility of a past event that is not clear in the present context:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">It <span class=\"strong\">could have been</span> a real tragedy.</span><br/> (Here, the modal <span class=\"italic\">could</span> adds the meaning of <span class=\"strong\">possibility</span>: <br/> It is possible that it was a real tragedy.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Lily's mother, Sarah, is convinced that her daughter would have frozen if it hadn't been for the puppies who stayed with her all through the night and kept her warm. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Lily decided she may be a vet when she gets older to honor those extraordinary animals that saved her life.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Past Perfect and Simple Past Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect</span> tense to identify and talk about an 'earlier past'.<br/> You use the <span class=\"strong\">Past Continuous</span> tense to talk about an action that was happening at a time before now.<br/> You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> to talk about a finished action that happened at a specific time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect</span> tense.<br/><br/>  The structure of the <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect</span> is:<br/><br/>  Subject + had + past participle<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">When I arrived at the party, Vanessa <span class=\"strong\">had</span> already <span class=\"strong\">gone</span> home. </span><br/> Which event happened first? Vanessa went home.<br/> Which event happened later? I arrived at the party.<br/><br/>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect</span> tense (not <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span>) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Until recently, detectives <span class=\"strong\">had used</span> a limited number of tools to help them solve crimes. </span><br/> Detectives used a limited number of tools from the past until recently. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A five-year-old girl was found safe and sound 12 hours after she had disappeared from her home in St. Simon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Lily Jackson had wandered away from her home on Friday afternoon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " She had worn light clothing and did not have gloves or a hat with her. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "baffled", "type": "name"}, {"content": "confused; unable to understand or explain something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's the kind of story that leaves you baffled and perplexed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about an unbelievable event.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to curl up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to sit or lie down with your legs and arms bent close to your body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Lily was curled up with Muffy, Ruffles, and Pluto, three of her four puppies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "extraordinary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "beyond what is usual; exceptional and surprising", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Those extraordinary animals saved her life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "field", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a piece of open land in the country", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She was looking for her puppy who had run into a field near her house.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to honor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show special respect and recognition", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Lily became a vet to honor the animals that saved her life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "light clothing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "clothes that are not heavy; comfortable clothing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Light clothing is appropriate for spring.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "perplexed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "confused and worried", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The girl's story left me baffled and perplexed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to snuggle", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to lie close to another being looking for warmth or affection", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She was saved from freezing to death by snuggling with three puppies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "uncanny", "type": "name"}, {"content": " mysterious; strange and difficult to describe", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was really uncanny to hear the dog had survived the catastrophe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to wander", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to walk around an area with no specific destination", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Lily Jackson had wandered away from her home on Friday afternoon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Tell a partner about an animal story like the one in the dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online and find a story (in English) about an animal saving a human.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the story and write down some of the key events.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Retell the story using your notes and past tenses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about about what might/could have happened if the animal had not been there", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read about life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write notes on life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use the noted to talk about life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about possibility and certainty.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about coincidences, strange events, and superstitions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about possibility and certainty.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about life experiences. ", "type": "Learning Out